+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-fix-single-use-coupon-giveback/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+## Context
+
+`Coupons.use(code, order)` stores the order id in `#usedBy`; `Coupons.giveBack(code, order)` deletes the entry only when the stored id equals `order`. `OrderService.cancel` passes `order.customer`, so the ids never match.
+
+## Decision
+
+Pass `order.id` (the `id` argument) to `giveBack`. No change to `Coupons`; its ownership check stays, so cancelling an unrelated order cannot release a coupon. No money handling is involved and no dependencies are added.
+
+## Risks
+
+None beyond the one-argument change; non-single-use coupons are never tracked, so they are unaffected.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-fix-single-use-coupon-giveback/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-fix-single-use-coupon-giveback/proposal.md
