--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-fix-single-use-coupon-giveback/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+## Why
+
+A customer placed an order with a single-use welcome code, cancelled it within the window, and the code was then refused as "already used" on the corrected order. The README says a cancelled order gives its single-use coupon back. `Coupons.use` records the order id (e.g. ORD-0001) as the user, but `OrderService.cancel` calls `giveBack` with the customer name, which never matches, so the coupon is never released.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `OrderService.cancel` gives the coupon back using the order id, the same key `place` used.
+- Regression test: place with a single-use coupon, cancel, place again with the same code.
+
+Second report (€4.90 shipping on exactly €50.00 goods): investigated, not reproducible. `shippingCost` uses `goods >= 5000`, `priceOrder` passes the goods after every discount, and existing tests cover €49.99, €50.00 and a discounted basket reaching €50.00. Probes at exactly 5000 cents gave 0 shipping. The likely explanation is that the customer's goods were above €50.00 gross but below it after discounts (which the README treats as charged), or the order predates the earlier shipping fix. No code change is made for it; more detail (order number) is needed from support.
+
+## README business rules affected
+
+Discounts: "A single-use coupon can be used by one order only; if that order is cancelled, the coupon can be used again." and Orders: cancelling gives back its coupon. The code is brought in line; the README is unchanged.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `coupon-discounts`: adds the requirement that cancelling gives back a single-use coupon.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/orders.ts` (one argument) and `test/orders.test.ts` or `test/coupons.test.ts`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+Shipping bands and the free-shipping rule, VAT, other coupon rules, orders already cancelled before the fix (their coupons stay recorded as used in memory only; no data migration).
